@startuml job-state-machine
title social_publish_job — State Machine

[*] --> draft : create (rarely used,\nlegacy path)

state "draft" as DR {
  DR : initial state\n(unused in current flow)
}

state "approved" as AP {
  AP : draft → approved\n(also rarely used)
}

state "queued" as QU {
  QU : initial state for all new jobs\n(now / schedule / draft modes)
  QU : scheduledAt may be future or null
  QU : lockedAt = null
}

state "publishing" as PB {
  PB : lockedAt set\nworker (or sync caller)\nis executing
  PB : adapter.publish() in flight
}

state "published" as PR {
  PR : terminal success
  PR : publishedAt set
  PR : publication row exists
}

state "failed" as FL {
  FL : last attempt failed
  FL : lastError set
  FL : can be retried (→ queued)
  FL : or cancelled (terminal)
}

state "cancelled" as CN {
  CN : terminal
  CN : explicit operator action\nor system cancellation
}

' Transitions
DR --> AP : approve
DR --> CN : cancel
DR --> QU : direct enqueue (system)

AP --> QU : enqueue (executeJob)
AP --> CN : cancel

QU --> PB : tryAcquireLock\n(success)
QU --> CN : cancelPublishJob
QU --> FL : pre-flight validation\nfailure (rare)

PB --> PR : adapter succeeded
PB --> FL : adapter failed\n(retryable or terminal)

FL --> QU : retryPublishJob\n(operator click)
FL --> CN : cancelPublishJob

PR --> [*]
CN --> [*]

' Idempotent self-loops
QU --> QU : (no-op if already queued)
PB --> PB : (no-op if already locked)

note right of QU
  Retry policy:
  - 3 attempts max (default)
  - exp backoff [100,300,900,1500]ms
  - Only on transient errors (5xx, 429, 408)
end note

note right of FL
  retryPublishJob:
  - resets status to queued
  - clears lockedAt
  - increments attemptCount
  - re-runs executeJob
end note

note bottom of PB
  Lock prevents 2 workers
  from picking the same job.
  lockedAt = now() when acquired.
  Released on success/failure.
end note

@enduml
